The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (CRYPTO_CURVE25519 == y) 
    CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519_GENERIC = y;
if (CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519 == m) 
    // self-test code is enabled but architecture-specific implementations are not available
```
Reason:
The self-test code for Curve25519 was incorrectly controlled by the GENERIC option instead of the overall CURVE25519 option. This misalignment caused the self-test to be enabled even when the necessary architecture-specific implementations (like `curve25519_arch` and `curve25519_base_arch`) were not available, leading to undefined references during the build process.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
// Split the GENERIC module from the CURVE25519 module
// Now the self-test is only enabled when CURVE25519 is selected
```
Reason:
By separating the GENERIC module from the CURVE25519 module, the self-test is now correctly tied to the overall CURVE25519 option. This ensures that the self-test is only enabled when the necessary architecture-specific implementations are available, thus preventing the undefined reference errors during the build process.

